<Item XName="Notes" UserName="Notes" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT color=#ff0000&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt; &#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=5&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Antenna Polarization TRx Basic Test Example&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=4&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;************************************************&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Simulation Task &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;************************************************&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;This example shows how to generate the antenna pattern and scan&amp;nbsp;data&amp;nbsp;with AutomotiveRadar_AntennaPolarizationTx and AntennaPolarizationRx&amp;nbsp;model. Under&amp;nbsp;identical configurations, their output results&amp;nbsp;are also identical.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;One pattern plot example and two antenna scan examples are demonstrated in this workspace. &lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The different weighting window functions and scan mode can be selected from the parameter list.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;************************************************&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Workspace Description&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;There are three folders for this workspace:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1, PatternPlot_TargetScan&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;For antenna radiation pattern plotting, the target scan mode is applied to both AntennaPolarizationTx &amp;amp; Rx models. By design, both AntennaPolarizationTx and Rx models could ONLY use&amp;nbsp;externally imported&amp;nbsp;antenna patterns (in this example is from HFSS pattern file), and both models work under radar coordinates for angle definitions, the PhasedArrayTx model is applied for pattern result comparison.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To generate the angle sweeps, we firstly use&amp;nbsp;MathLang script models to realize target phi and theta sweeps under antenna coordinate definitions (Theta and Phi), then transform both angles into radar coordinates (elevation and azimuth). Then the angle sweeps are inserted into the target elevation and azimuth input ports of AntennaPolarizationTx and Rx models to generate the output pattern data in complex formats.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The desired output for Antenna Polarization Tx and Rx models&amp;nbsp;are H and V polarized patterns, and one MathLang model is designed to recombine the H/V components. Mathlang combination is easier to understand, but with lower simulation efficiency, so the SystemVue Math blocks are applied in shipping example.The recombined pattern&amp;nbsp;results are compared with PhasedArrayTx model, and&amp;nbsp;the corresponding&amp;nbsp;results are almost identical except for some rounding errors. For the Antenna Polarization Rx, the H/V pattern extraction and recombination&amp;nbsp;can&amp;nbsp;be realized in the same way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To view the patterns, we use two equations to&amp;nbsp;plot antenna patterns under&amp;nbsp;planar (UV)&amp;nbsp;and spherical coordinates, respectively.&amp;nbsp;For&amp;nbsp;both coordinate display modes,&amp;nbsp;Linear and dB formats are available.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;2, Circular_Scan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To demonstrate circular scanning capability, we set the AntennaPolarizationTx and Rx in circular scan mode and observe the output results. Multiple&amp;nbsp;circular scan&amp;nbsp;periods are shown.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;3, UniBiRaster_Scan&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To demonstrate&amp;nbsp;UniRaster and BiRaster&amp;nbsp;scanning capability, we set the AntennaPolarizationTx and Rx in&amp;nbsp;Uni/BiRaster scan modes and observe the output results. In this design we select the UniRaster mode to demonstrate flyback time and retrace time effects on scan results.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
